      "writtenOn": "2023-09-22T09:30:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately I think this is even more unsafe than it was.\nIf this struct is moved, the CBB will still be pointing to the old buf, with potentially disastrous consequences. You have a self-referential struct, which is tricky in Rust.\n\nI can see 2 options:\n- Create a struct with just the zeroized buffer, and only tranisently create the CBB in a single scope, very carefully, with a bunch of safety comments.\n- Do what you have now, but add PhantomPinned to FixedSizeCbb, and return Pin\u003cBox\u003cFixedSizeCbb\u003e\u003e.\n\n\nGiven currently you only use a CBB in privat_key(), where the buffer and the CBB only exist for the duration of the function, the former might be simplest; you don\u0027t yet need a safe Rust abstraction over CBB.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 110,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 113,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "84f284e9c61c058e6dc0b4476f412e22e5842fab",
